2.2 Navigation integration — important constraints
Waze limitation
Waze does not provide a supported general-purpose embeddable in-app map view for a third-party Compose application. Integrate Waze through supported Waze deep links / intents to search or start navigation, then return to this app. Do not scrape, WebView-wrap, mirror or claim to embed the Waze app.

•	Provide a prominent Open Waze action and destination hand-off using supported Waze URL/deep-link parameters. Handle Waze not installed and unsupported destinations gracefully.
•	Provide optional in-app map using a supported SDK (Google Maps SDK or another provider) with its own API key, billing, terms and attribution. Map is a separate provider integration, not Waze.
•	Do not make Google Maps SDK a hard dependency for OBD operation. App must work when map key is absent or network is unavailable.
•	Explore Android Auto as a separate future integration using approved Android for Cars App Library templates and categories. Android Auto is not an unrestricted screen-mirroring surface; custom Compose horizontal pages cannot simply be projected.
•	Support external app hand-off and app resume; preserve OBD session state carefully and reconnect if Android suspends the process.
