Decoder rule
Implement decoders from the relevant SAE/ISO standard and test vectors. This table is an illustrative starter list, not a complete PID catalogue. Some PIDs are optional, have different payload lengths or are not supported by the Sportage ECU.

4.5 Polling strategy
Priority	Examples	Initial policy
P0 / cockpit	RPM, speed, coolant, voltage if available	Fast enough for a responsive display, but adapter-safe; target ~2–5 updates/sec per critical group, not per PID.
P1 / engine	Load, throttle, MAP/MAF, fuel trims	~1 update/sec or slower; rotate requests.
P2 / slow diagnostics	O2, Mode 06, readiness, VIN	On demand or periodic slow refresh; never compete with P0.
P3 / background	History, maintenance, export	No live OBD polling.

Measure actual command round-trip time. Adapt the polling schedule to adapter performance, number of supported ECUs and transport. Provide a low-bandwidth mode for clone adapters.
 
