Do not invent addresses, PIDs or diagnostic session sequences. Public documentation may not expose proprietary Kia procedures. The app should show 'not supported / not verified' instead of a false green check.
5.3 DTC knowledge base
Create a local DTC catalogue with generic SAE code definitions plus optional verified Kia-specific extensions. Fields: code, system, title, plain-language explanation, severity, symptoms, common causes, diagnostic checks, source URL/document, applicability, confidence, last verified date and whether the code is generic or manufacturer-specific.
For P0420, show catalyst-system efficiency below threshold as a generic description. Offer a structured diagnostic checklist: check exhaust leaks, fuel trims, upstream/downstream sensor behaviour, misfire history and relevant service information. Never conclude the catalytic converter is defective from code alone.
5.4 Research and source provenance
Create a /docs/research directory in the project. Keep a source register with title, URL, date accessed, what it supports, vehicle applicability and confidence. Prefer Kia service information/TSBs, SAE/ISO standards, official Android docs, official Waze/Google Maps docs and reputable open-source libraries. Treat forum posts and GitHub reverse-engineering as leads, not proof.
 
