7.3 State and data model
Use typed domain models. Do not pass raw strings through the UI. Represent unavailable, unsupported, stale, invalid and live states explicitly.
sealed interface ReadingState<out T> {
    data class Live<T>(
        val value: T,
        val unit: String,
        val timestampMillis: Long,
        val source: DataSource
    ) : ReadingState<T>
    data class Stale<T>(
        val lastValue: T,
        val lastUpdatedMillis: Long
    ) : ReadingState<T>
    data object Unsupported : ReadingState<Nothing>
    data object Unavailable : ReadingState<Nothing>
    data class Error(val reason: String) : ReadingState<Nothing>
}

enum class DataSource { OBD_STANDARD, KIA_ENHANCED, GPS, USER_INPUT, CALCULATED, DEMO }

data class VehicleSession(
    val vehicleId: String,
    val adapterId: String?,
    val protocol: String?,
    val connectedAtMillis: Long?,
    val state: ConnectionState
)

7.4 Foreground/background behaviour
Use a foreground service only when an active user-started vehicle session genuinely needs ongoing telemetry while the app is backgrounded. Provide a persistent notification and stop control. Respect Android background execution and Bluetooth restrictions. Do not keep scanning or polling indefinitely after the user disconnects or exits the session.
 
