9. Safety and responsible diagnostics
Safety boundary
This is a monitoring and diagnostic aid, not a safety-certified instrument cluster. Do not present OBD speed as the vehicle's legally authoritative speedometer. Do not encourage phone interaction while driving. All detailed diagnostics, code clearing, configuration, performance tests and exports should be parked-only or require a deliberate safety gate.

•	Use GPS speed only as a secondary display and label its source; do not replace factory speedometer.
•	Sensor thresholds must be configurable and sourced; account for operating conditions.
•	Never state that a component is safe or defective based on one PID.
•	Before clearing DTCs, explain data/readiness loss and ask for confirmation.
•	Do not expose Mode 08 control, raw CAN write or proprietary security access in the initial release.
•	Do not provide ECU flashing, immobilizer, key programming, airbag activation/deactivation or emissions defeat functions.
 
